\title{ucmtools: Bayesian Inference of Unobserved Components Models}
\description{
Bayesian trend-cycle decompositions of one or more time series by unobserved components models: a random walk or smooth trend with an optional drift and breaks in it, a stationary autoregressive cycle, an optional irregular component, and shocks that are independent, correlated, stochastically volatile or skewed. The posterior is simulated by the Gibbs samplers of the 'BayesTS' library, after Grant and Chan (2017) and Huang, Luo and Wang (2026). Forecasts, the integrated log likelihood and model comparison work through the shared layer of package 'bayests'.
}
